Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/43] Dielectric: separate reflection roughness (for hdPbrt)

"hdpbrtreflectionroughness" / "hdpbrtreflection{u,v}roughness": the
reflection lobe gets its own GGX distribution, the transmission keeps
"roughness" (MaterialX standard_surface transmission_extra_roughness and
pbrlib layer(R over T) with different roughnesses). Split lobes are picked
by the macro-surface Fresnel (clamped to [0.05, 0.95]) and sample their own
microfacets. hdpbrttopweight uses the reflection's roughness, and for split
lobes seen from inside a reflection albedo table that includes total
internal reflection; otherwise the wide transmission adds to a TIR'd
reflection and gains energy.
